---
import SectionHeader from "./SectionHeader.astro";
---

<section class="bg-surface-subtle">
  <div class="container">
    <SectionHeader num="11" title="FAQ" />
    <div class="faq-list">
      <div class="faq-item rounded-xl overflow-hidden border border-surface-muted">
        <div class="faq-q-hover faq-q px-5 py-4 text-[16px] font-semibold flex justify-between items-center cursor-pointer select-none transition-colors duration-200 bg-surface-base">
          What is Mizu?
          <span class="text-xs transition-transform duration-200 text-foreground-tertiary font-mono">&rarr;</span>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-a text-sm leading-relaxed text-foreground-secondary">
          A constraint-based design token system for building coherent interfaces. One primary navy, one blue accent, neutral grays. It provides the color, typography, spacing, and component foundations that any project can adopt.
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item rounded-xl overflow-hidden border border-surface-muted">
        <div class="faq-q-hover faq-q px-5 py-4 text-[16px] font-semibold flex justify-between items-center cursor-pointer select-none transition-colors duration-200 bg-surface-base">
          What can it produce?
          <span class="text-xs transition-transform duration-200 text-foreground-tertiary font-mono">&rarr;</span>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-a text-sm leading-relaxed text-foreground-secondary">
          Design system documentation, landing pages, component libraries, data dashboards, and documentation portals. The token system is framework-agnostic and works with any CSS-in-JS or static CSS approach.
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item rounded-xl overflow-hidden border border-surface-muted">
        <div class="faq-q-hover faq-q px-5 py-4 text-[16px] font-semibold flex justify-between items-center cursor-pointer select-none transition-colors duration-200 bg-surface-base">
          How do I set it up?
          <span class="text-xs transition-transform duration-200 text-foreground-tertiary font-mono">&rarr;</span>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-a text-sm leading-relaxed text-foreground-secondary">
          Install via npm or yarn —             <code class="px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-xs bg-surface-muted">npm install @mizu-ui/tokens</code>. Import the tokens and use them directly in your preferred styling solution. No build tools required.
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item rounded-xl overflow-hidden border border-surface-muted">
        <div class="faq-q-hover faq-q px-5 py-4 text-[16px] font-semibold flex justify-between items-center cursor-pointer select-none transition-colors duration-200 bg-surface-base">
          Can I extend the palette?
          <span class="text-xs transition-transform duration-200 text-foreground-tertiary font-mono">&rarr;</span>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-a text-sm leading-relaxed text-foreground-secondary">
          Yes, but keep the core constraints: one primary, one accent, neutral grays. Additional product-specific tokens can sit alongside the core system, but should never override the foundational palette.
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
